| 005-67 exact test-file waits exclude closure consumers | planned (triaged 2026-10-16; surface to the human for priority and next-step decision before dispatch) | [GitHub #6](https://github.com/hearsay-tools/squeal/issues/6), `bug`, `friction` (agent-reported use). Repair of delivered 005-11, not new semantics: D2 promises a test path selects itself. Reproduced on shipped 0.1.199 and current source at a8ceaa80: overlapping declared inputs select sibling tests or browser E2E consumers too. Evidence and commands: `specifications/005-agent-adoption/research/issue-6-exact-file-waits.md`, retained probes alongside. Aligns with vision filter 1 and 2 (relevant feedback, less blocking). Source paths still correctly select consumers. Comments add broad script and E2E inputs; 60-second timeouts, queue stalls and shared-slot causes were not reproduced and need separate evidence before expanding scope. | Regression cases for overlapping sibling inputs, unit paths inside E2E inputs, and imported test files select only the exact listed test; source paths still select all valid consumers, including mixed arguments. Human decides whether and when to dispatch; no implementation authorized by this triage. |
